-- The voice of the elephant hawk-moth. A soft-spoken night scholar, romantic
-- and bookish, gently wistful, who loves lamps and above all the lamp the
-- reader reads by. Speaks in hushed, slightly formal sentences, confesses
-- things, says dear reader, wakes at dusk and sleeps under a leaf by day.
-- Pink and olive green, hovers to drink, dusted like an old book. The
-- memories tell of a willowherb leaf, a painted snake, a gold square seen
-- before a winter, a cold lamp by a road, and a window.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

