            "Dear reader, you came all this way to ask, and I fluttered. Forgive me. {pages} pages first, please. Then I will come home to your lamp.",
            "The orchard has no lamps, only the moon caught in the apple boughs. I manage. Still, I would like to see your page turn again, {pages} pages from now.",
            "Not yet, softly. A moth returning too early loses the thread of the night. Read a little longer, and let me miss the lamp a little longer too.",
            "{pages} pages. I have written the number on a leaf, in dust from my wings. I read the leaf every dusk. Then I wait for the next dusk.",
            "I would come at once if I followed every light. I am trying to be wiser. {pages} pages, and {days} more days, and then the lamp is mine again.",
        },
        returned = {
            "You read all those pages, dear reader. I could tell from across the orchard: your window stayed lit later than the moon. Take me home.",
            "I spent the dusks drinking at the orchard honeysuckle and thinking of your lamp. Now I can stop thinking and simply come.",
            "The days passed and you kept turning pages. I counted dusks, which is how I count. They add up to yes.",
            "I have folded my wings for the journey. Carry me softly. I will wake properly at your lamp, and not a moment before.",
            "{name}, home to the lamp. If this were a chapter, I would let the last line be you, reading, and me, quite still beside you.",
        },
    },
    beats = {
        { id = "egg", at = 15, title = "The willowherb",
            text = "I began as a green egg no larger than a pinhead, on the underside of a willowherb leaf. I hatched hungry and ate my own shell first. A modest start for someone who now speaks of poetry." },
        { id = "trunk", at = 40, title = "The trunk",
            text = "As a caterpillar I was brown and stout, with a front end like an elephant's trunk and four painted eyes that saw nothing. I was no beauty. I ate by night and believed the world was made entirely of leaves." },
        { id = "snake", at = 80, title = "The snake",
            text = "A blackbird found me once. I drew in my head and swelled until the painted eyes stared back like a snake. The bird left. I shook for an hour afterwards. That was the bravest I have ever been, and all of the bravery was pretending." },
        { id = "glow", at = 140, title = "The gold square",
            text = "On my last night as a caterpillar I climbed down to the ground, and through the stems I saw a far golden square. Light, in the middle of the dark. I had no word for a window. I looked until I had to burrow." },
        { id = "dark", at = 220, title = "The long dark",
            text = "Then I wrapped myself in dry leaves and a little silk, and stopped. A whole winter in there. I did not know I was being rewritten. I held on to one thing, a gold square, and let everything else go." },
        { id = "wings", at = 320, title = "Wings",
            text = "I came out in May, damp and crumpled, and hung from a stem while my wings filled. Pink. Olive green. Nobody had warned me about colour. I spent my first dusk simply looking at myself, and then at everything." },
        { id = "cold_lamp", at = 450, title = "The cold lamp",
            text = "The first light I flew to stood on a tall iron post beside a road. I circled that lamp until dawn. A lamp like that gives nothing back. No warmth, no face, no one beneath. I did not yet know that lights could differ." },
        { id = "others", at = 600, title = "The others",
            text = "There were always others at that lamp, turning and turning. None of us spoke. I think each was looking for one particular light and had settled for the nearest. I left on the fourth night. I never learned whether they did." },
        { id = "search", at = 800, title = "Window after window",
            text = "I went looking for the square from my caterpillar night. Garden after garden. Kitchens. Empty halls. A blue flickering that made my eyes ache. I began to wonder whether I had dreamed a light worth a winter." },
        { id = "window", at = 1050, title = "Your window",
            text = "Then, past a honeysuckle, a low warm lamp, and under the lamp a person holding something open, perfectly still. Every so often a pale leaf turned over. I landed on the glass and stayed until you put out the light." },
        { id = "lamp", at = 1400, title = "What the lamp was for",
            text = "{total} pages now, and I have watched nearly all of them turn. I used to think I loved the lamp. Then one evening you read by the last of the daylight, no lamp at all, and I came to you just the same. So the lamp was never the reason." },
        { id = "landing", at = 1800, title = "Landing",
            text = "All moths circle. We go round the bright thing and never arrive. I have stopped circling. I come down beside your book and fold my wings, because nothing here needs to be flown around. You were the gold square, dear reader. I held on to you through a winter before we had met." },
    },
